// Test: Function inlining optimization
// Small functions called multiple times should be inlined to eliminate CALL/RETN overhead.
// This program defines small helper functions and calls them multiple times.
// The inliner should inline renderPoint (2 stmts, 3+ call sites) and addTen (1 stmt, 2+ call sites).

ClrDraw

// Small helper - single statement, called multiple times from the loop
Function addTen(val)
  Return val + 10
End

// Small helper - 2 statements, called multiple times  
Function doubleIt(val)
  Return val * 2
End

// Test inlining through a loop
For i = 0 To 5
  x = addTen(i)       // Should be inlined
  y = doubleIt(x)     // Should be inlined
  // Use results on screen
  PxlOn(x, y, 10)
Next

// Display a result to verify behavior
result = addTen(5)    // Should produce 15
Text(0, 0, "Inline test OK", result)